Description: Resolve MPP runtime firmware outside PPA build chroots
 The K3 VPU firmware is a real architecture-specific runtime package from the
 official SpacemiT K3 archive, not a build tool. Keep the k1x/k3x alternative
 as Recommends so normal apt installs retain the default firmware dependency,
 while Launchpad build chroots can install MPP development files without a
 hard runtime-firmware dependency. No decoder source or runtime hardware
 preference is changed and no dummy firmware package is provided.
Author: Yeqin Su <hougelangley1987@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-23

--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -11,7 +11,8 @@
 Package: mpp
 Architecture: any
 Multi-Arch: no
-Depends: k1x-vpu-firmware|k3x-vpu-firmware, ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
+Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
+Recommends: k1x-vpu-firmware|k3x-vpu-firmware
 Description: auto-generated package by debmake
